The repo has already found the right primitive: `/f/<slug>` is now an actual mini-stage with VRM performance, timed reactions, voting and a reply/remix path rather than a dead audio share.  The next move is to make **RESPOND the dominant outcome**, not one option among KEEP/CUT / MAKE YOUR OWN / PASS IT ON.

The external precedent is strong: YouTube explicitly preserves remix source lineage, lets remixes themselves be remixed, and attributes remix traffic back to the source. ([Google Help][1]) Also, shared Freak links should remain ordinary HTTPS URLs so the exact same URL can later deep-link into the iOS app through Universal Links while still working on the web. ([Apple Developer][2])

Here is the product spec I would implement.

# Freak Town Share → Watch → Respond Loop

## Product thesis

The shared Freak is not a webpage.

It is a **60-second challenge sent from one person to another**.

The entire product loop should be:

```text
MAKE FREAK
    ↓
SEND LINK
    ↓
friend taps
    ↓
WATCH 60s
    ↓
YOUR TURN
    ↓
RESPOND
    ↓
watch your reply
    ↓
SEND BACK
    ↓
repeat
```

The ideal interaction requires:

```text
0 account creation
0 navigation
0 understanding of Freak Town
1 tap to watch
1 tap to respond
```

The viewer can discover the broader product afterwards.

---

# 1. The shared link

Current:

```text
freak.town/f/<slug>
```

Keep this as the immutable short/share ID.

But introduce human-readable canonical identity underneath it.

Recommended URL hierarchy:

```text
freak.town/@thomas
```

Creator.

```text
freak.town/@thomas/peg
```

Permanent character page.

```text
freak.town/@thomas/peg/farting-dog
```

Permanent performance/set.

And:

```text
freak.town/f/7QxK2
```

Short immutable share alias.

`/f/7QxK2` resolves the performance and can redirect/render using the canonical URL.

This gives us:

```text
CREATOR
@thomas

    ↓ owns

CHARACTER
Peg

    ↓ performs many

SETS
farting-dog
divorce-court
pigeon-911
tesco
```

Do not make:

```text
/thomas/fartingdog
```

mean a character sometimes and a set other times.

Use:

```text
/@creator/character
/@creator/character/set
```

The `@` also protects namespaces such as:

```text
/live
/studio
/api
/f
/about
```

from colliding with usernames.

Handles/slugs should be backed internally by immutable IDs.

If someone renames a handle later:

```text
old URL → permanent redirect → new URL
```

Never allow an already-shared Freak link to die.

