# 2. WhatsApp / iMessage / Discord preview

The preview itself needs to make you want to tap.

Not:

```text
Martin — Freak Town
AI comedy performance
```

Instead make it look like a collectible character card.

Example:

```text
┌────────────────────────────┐
│                            │
│             PEG            │
│          [portrait]        │
│                            │
│   PARANOID PIGEON          │
│   DIVORCE LAWYER           │
│                            │
│             0:58           │
│                 FREAK TOWN │
└────────────────────────────┘
```

Metadata:

```text
TITLE
Peg — Farting Dog

DESCRIPTION
A paranoid pigeon divorce lawyer.
58 seconds. Watch it, then answer back.

IMAGE
purpose-built 1200×630 share card

URL
canonical performance URL
```

Use proper Open Graph:

```text
og:title
og:type = video.other
og:url
og:image
og:image:width
og:image:height
og:image:alt
og:description
og:site_name
video:duration
```

The current watch page uses `music.song`; that should become `video.other`. The Open Graph spec defines `video.other` specifically for video that does not fit its movie/TV categories, and `og:url` is intended as the object's permanent canonical identity. ([GitHub][3]) ([GitHub][4])

Later also produce:

```text
share-card.webp
share-video.mp4
```

from the same performance artifact.

