# 19. The metrics that matter

For every shared performance record:

```text
share_created
share_opened
play_started
25%
50%
75%
completed
laugh_count
respond_tray_seen
response_seed_changed
response_edited
response_started
response_generated
response_watched
response_shared
```

Then calculate:

```text
open → play
play → complete
complete → respond
respond → generated
generated → share
```

The killer number is:

```text
K = average new shared responses
    created by each shared performance
```

If:

```text
K > 1
```

the loop can compound.

Also log:

```text
response_depth
branch_factor
time_to_reply
same-pair reply count
```

Because a five-message rivalry between two friends is probably more valuable than five unrelated views.

---

# 20. Performance should never wait for 3D

For a viral shared link, responsiveness matters more than renderer purity.

Load order:

```text
HTML + metadata
      ↓
portrait
      ↓
audio
      ↓
PLAY READY
      ↓
VRM + renderer upgrade in background
```

If the 10MB VRM isn't ready:

```text
portrait performs with subtle motion
audio begins anyway
```

Then fade the 3D performer in when ready.

Never show:

```text
Loading model...
```

for five seconds before the friend can hear the joke.

Eventually the share page can use a deterministically pre-rendered MP4 as the ultra-reliable playback surface while reactions/UI stay live, with the exact same performance object feeding it.

