# North-star behavior

Someone sends:

```text
freak.town/f/7QxK2
```

to their friend on WhatsApp.

Friend taps.

Peg appears.

They tap once.

Peg does his ridiculous 58-second minute.

At the end the interface says:

```text
YOUR TURN
```

with an already-funny comeback sitting there.

They tap:

```text
RESPOND
```

Freak Town invents Gerald the exhausted employment-lawyer crab and performs the answer.

They laugh.

They hit:

```text
SEND BACK
```

Their friend receives Gerald.

And underneath both links, Freak Town now knows:

```text
Peg → Gerald
```

That is the viral object.

**Not the episode. Not the website. Not even the set.**

The viral object is the **conversation between Freaks**.

One additional thing I would prioritize very early: when a reply comes back to one of your characters, give the owner a notification like **“Gerald responded to Peg.”** That turns a shared link from a disposable joke into an unfinished conversation, which is exactly what makes people reopen it.

